{{!-- A route's name, and nothing else.

      Core's own page header carries a heading LEVEL and a "Display Page Title" switch, because a
      text page is a section of a document and those decide how it folds into the table of
      contents. A route is not a section of anything: it is one path between two points, drawn as
      a ruled block whose title is always its name. Both controls were therefore two ways to make
      the page render wrong, and neither answered a question a Warden has.

      The name field itself stays — it is what the map pin, the journey's head and both endpoint
      selects read. --}}
<header class="journal-header">
    {{formInput fields.name value=name classes="title"
                aria=(object label=(localize "JOURNALENTRYPAGE.FIELDS.name.label"))
                placeholder=(localize "JOURNALENTRYPAGE.FIELDS.name.label")}}
</header>
